<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βυσσοδομεύω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δομέω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>build in the deep</i>:
			hence, <i>brood over</i> a thing <i>in the depth of one's soul,
				ponder deeply</i>; <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, always in bad sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὰ φρεσὶ βυσσοδόμευον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.66
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύθους β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.676
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλον φρεσὶ β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			: also in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργὴν β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cal.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ βυσσοδομευόμενα</span>
			<i>secret designs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.11
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βυρσ-δομέω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1513.46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
